# Agent memory protocol (this repo)

Cross-chat memory is **not automatic**. Use the files below as the source of truth.

## At the start of every non-trivial task

1. Read `.cursor/CONTEXT.md` (living project memory).
2. Read `.cursor/rules/pulse-desk-linkage.mdc` before any sectors/map/load change.
3. Prefer fixing regressions over “simplifying away” prior fixes (especially after user asks to revert one feature).

## Before finishing (or when user asks to ship / push)

Update `.cursor/CONTEXT.md` with:

- What changed and **why**
- Current live URL + asset/SW version if bumped
- Open bugs / known traps
- Explicit **Do not regress** bullets for this session’s work

Keep CONTEXT.md short (aim ≤120 lines). Oldest resolved noise can be deleted; keep active constraints.

## Hard bans

- Never revert linkage/stub/map-week fixes in isolation — keep coexisting capabilities (see linkage rule).
- Never claim “remembered” something that is not written into CONTEXT.md or a rule.
- If unsure about prior intent, read CONTEXT.md + recent `git log` before editing.
